hadiths[165]{hadithnumber,text}:
"6766","Ali bin Muhammad Al-Masisi told us, he said: Khalaf bin Tamim told us, he said: Zaida told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Ubaid bin Nudhaylah, on the authority of Al-Mughirah bin Shu’bah, that a woman hit her partner with a tent pole and killed her while she was pregnant, so he was brought Therein the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, then the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, made a judgment on the killer’s relatives to pay blood money, and to pay blood money to the fetus, and he said Her ring: Is it the one who has neither food nor drink nor shouted, should he begin? ! Something like this was delayed, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Should I kneel like the Bedouins do?!” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6767","Muhammad bin Qudamah Al-Masisi told us, he said: Jarir told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Ubaid bin Nudaila Al-Khuza’i, On the authority of Mughirah bin Shu’bah, he said: A woman was struck by a pillar of a tent while she was pregnant, and she killed her. The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, made He, peace be upon him, handed over the blood money of the murdered woman to the killer’s clan, and compensation for what was in her stomach. A man from the murderer’s clan said, “He was fined the blood money from someone who did not Did he eat, drink, or initiate? ! Something like that was delayed, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Should I kneel like the Bedouins kneel?” So he imposed on them the blood money. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6768","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Abdul Rahman told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Ubaid bin Nudayla, on the authority of Al-Mughirah bin Shu’bah, that two females, one of them hitting the other with a tent, killed her. “So the Messenger of God decided May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, the blood money must be paid on the woman’s neck, and he will make up for what is in her stomach with a vengeance. The Bedouin said: You will fine me for not eating or drinking. Did he not shout and start? ! An example of that appeared, and he said: “Should I prostrate like the prostration of pre-Islamic times?” And he judged what was in her stomach by surprise. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6769","Ali bin Saeed bin Masruq told us, he said: Yahya bin Abi Zaida told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, On the authority of Ubaid bin Nudayla, on the authority of Al-Mughirah bin Shu’bah, he said: A woman from Banu Lahyan hit her husband with a pillar of Fustat. So she killed her, and there was a lamb on the victim. “Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, made a judgment on the killer’s wife to pay the blood money and what was in her stomach.” \Bangs\"""""""
"6770","Suwayd bin Nasr told us, he said: Abdullah, who is Ibn Al-Mubarak, told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Mansur, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Ubaid bin Nudayla, on the authority of Al-Mughirah bin Shu’bah, that two women were under a man from Hudhayl, and one of them threw a pole at the other. Fustat, then it dropped, so they disputed to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: How can we call out one who neither shouted, nor began, nor drank, nor Did he eat? ! Then the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Should I kneel like the Bedouins kneel?” So he ruled that the woman should be blinded. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6771","Mahmoud bin Ghaylan told us, he said: Abu Dawud told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Mansour, he said: I heard Ibrahim, on the authority of Ubaid. Ibn Nudhaylah, on the authority of Al-Mughirah Ibn Shu’bah, that a man from Hudhayl had two wives, and one of them threw the other at the pillar of Al-Fusat. So she miscarried, and it was said: Have you seen the one who neither ate nor drank nor shouted, so he started? ! He said: “Should I prostrate like the prostration of a Bedouin?” So the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, ruled that whether a male or female male or female slave should be ignorant, and it would be given to a virtuous woman. The woman.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Sulaiman al-Amash sent him"
"6772","Muhammad bin Rafi’ told us, he said: Mus’ab told us, he said: Dawud, who is Ibn Nusayr al-Tai, told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: A woman hit her with a stone while she was pregnant, killing her. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, made what was in her womb a surprise, and made Her mind is on her nerves, so they said: Shall I be fined who does not drink, eat, or entertain himself? ! Something like that appeared, and he said: “Should I kneel like the Bedouins? That is what I am telling you.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6773","Ahmad bin Uthman bin Hakim Kufi told us, saying: Amr bin Talha al-Qannad told us, on the authority of Asbat, on the authority of Samak bin Harb, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, said: There were two neighbouring women, and there was a commotion between them, and one of them threw a stone at the other, causing her to fall. A boy whose hair had sprouted died, and the woman died, so the blood money was imposed on the woman, and her uncle said: O Messenger of God, she has miscarried a boy who... His hair grew back, and the father of the killer said: He is a liar. By God, he did not initiate, nor drink, nor eat, so something like him becomes apparent, said the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, peace and blessings of God be upon him: “Should I prostrate like the prostration of pre-Islamic times, and its soothsaying? Ibn Abbas said: One of them was Malika, and the other was Umm Ghaytif. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6774","Al-Abbas bin Abdul-Azeem told us, he said: Al-Dahhak bin Mukhlid told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, he said: Abu Al-Zubair told me that He heard Jabir saying: “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, has decreed upon every stomach a burden, and it is not permissible for a master to take charge of a Muslim without his permission.” \"" 6775"""""
"6775","'Amr ibn 'Uthman and Muhammad ibn al-Musaffa narrated to us, saying: Al-Walid narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from 'Amr ibn Shu'ayb, from his father, from his grandfather, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""Whoever practices medicine while he was not known to have knowledge of medicine before that, he is liable (for damages)."" Mahmud ibn Khalid informed me, saying: Al-Walid narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from 'Amr ibn Shu'ayb, from his grandfather, the like of it exactly."
"6776","Harun bin Abdullah told me, he said: Sufyan told us, he said: Abd al-Malik bin Abjar told me, on the authority of Iyad bin Laqit, on the authority of Abu Rimthah, he said: I came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, with my father, and he said: “Who is this with you?” He said: My son bears witness to him. He said: As for him, he does not He commits injustice against you, but you do not commit injustice against him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6777","Mahmoud bin Ghaylan told us, he said: Bishr bin Al-Sari told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Aswad bin Hilal, on the authority of Tha'labah bin Zahudham al-Yarbu'i said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was giving a sermon, and some people from the Ansar came and said: O Messenger of God, Banu Tha’labah bin Yarubu’ killed so-and-so in pre-Islamic times, so the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said and shouted in his voice: “Will not a soul be spared? \other\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""""
"6778","Ahmad bin Sulaiman told us, he said: Muawiyah bin Hisham told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ash’ath bin Abi Ash-Sha’atha, on the authority of Al-Aswad bin Hilal, on the authority of Tha’labah bin Zuhdam, who said: A group of Banu Tha’labah came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, while he was giving a sermon, and a man said: O Messenger of God, these are Banu Tha’labah bin Yarubu’. They killed so-and-so, a man from the companions of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. Then the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Peace and blessings of God be upon him: “Let no soul oppress another.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6779","Mahmoud bin Ghaylan told us, he said: Abu Dawud told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Ash’ath bin Abi Al-Sha’atha’, he said: I heard Al-Aswad bin Hilal narrated, on the authority of a man from Banu Tha’labah bin Yarubu’, that people from Banu Tha’labah came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. Then a man said: O Messenger of God, these Banu Tha’labah bin Yarubu’ killed so-and-so, a man from the companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. So the Prophet said May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “Let no soul oppress another.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6780","Abu Dawud Al-Harrani told us, he said: Abu Attab Sahlin Hammad Al-Basri told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Al-Ash’ath ibn Sulaym, on the authority of Al-Aswad ibn Hilal, and the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, had learned on the authority of a man from Banu Tha’labah ibn Yarubu’ that people from Banu Tha'labah attacked a man from the companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and a man with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: These are Banu Alopecia killed so-and-so, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Let no soul harm another.” Shu`bah said: That is, no one will be taken by force, and God knows best. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6781","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Abu Awanah told us, on the authority of Al-Ash’ath bin Sulaym, on the authority of his father, on the authority of a man from the Banu Yarubu’, He said: I came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, while he was speaking, and a man said: O Messenger of God, these are the Banu Tha’labah bin Yarubu’, who They injured so-and-so, and the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “No, meaning, one soul harms another.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6782","Hanad bin Al-Sirri told us, in his hadith, on the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of his father, on the authority of a man from the Banu Yarubu’, who said: We came The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was speaking to the people, and some people came up to him and said: O Messenger of God, these are the sons of so-and-so who killed so-and-so. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Let no soul harm another.”"
"6783","Yusuf bin Issa Al-Marwazi informed us, he said: Al-Fadl bin Musa informed us, he said: Yazid informed us, and he is the son of Ziyad bin Abi Al-Ja’d, On the authority of Jami` bin Shaddad, on the authority of Tariq al-Muharbi, that a man said: O Messenger of God, these are Banu Tha`labah who killed so-and-so in Pre-Islamic times, so take our vengeance.” He raised his hands until I saw the whites of his armpits, and he said: “A mother should not commit injustice against a child” twice."
"6784","Ahmad bin Ibrahim bin Muhammad told us, he said: Ibn Aidh told us, he said: Al-Haytham bin Humaid told us, he said: Al-Alaa told me He is Ibn Al-Harith, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “made a judgment on the eye.” For a blind eye that is plain in its place if it is erased, a third of its blood money, and for a hand that is paralyzed if it is cut off, a third of its blood money, and for a black tooth if It was taken away, a third of her blood money.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6785","Muhammad bin Muawiyah bin Malij told us, saying: Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Hussein Al-Mu’allim, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of His father, on the authority of his grandfather, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “In the teeth, there are five like those of camels.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6786","Al-Hussein bin Mansour told us, he said: Hafs bin Abdul Rahman told us, he said: Saeed bin Abi Arouba told us, on the authority of Matar, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Teeth are equal, five by five.”"
"6787","Abu Al-Ash’ath told us, he said: Khaled told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Masruq ibn Aws, on the authority of Abu Musa, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. He said: “There are ten in the fingers.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6788","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Yazid told us, and he is Ibn Zuray’, he said: Sa’id told us, on the authority of Ghalib al-Tamar, on the authority of Masruq bin Aws. On the authority of Abu Musa Al-Ash’ari, that the Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The fingers are equal, ten, ten.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6789","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Muhammad bin Jafar told us, he said: Saeed bin Abi Orouba told us, on the authority of Ghalib al-Tamar, on the authority of Humaid bin Hilal, On the authority of Masruq ibn Aws, on the authority of Abu Musa, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “The fingers are equal, ten.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6790","Al-Hussein bin Mansour told us, he said: Hafs bin Abdul Rahman Balkhi told us, on the authority of Saeed, on the authority of Ghalib Al-Tamar, on the authority of Humaid bin Hilal, on the authority of Masruq ibn Aws, on the authority of Abu Musa, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ruled that the fingers are equal, ten of \camels\"""""""
"6791","Al-Hussein bin Mansour told us, he said: Abdullah bin Numayr told us, he said: Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, When the letter was found that was with the family of Amr ibn Hazm, which they mentioned that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, wrote for them, they found In it: “And among the fingers there are ten, ten.”"
"6792","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Yahya bin Saeed told us, he said: Shu`bah told us, he said: Qatada told me, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “This and this are the same, meaning: the little finger and the thumb.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6793","Nasr bin Ali bin Nasr told us, he said: Yazid told us, and he is bin Zurai’, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “This one and that one are the same, the thumb and the little finger.”"
"6794","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Yazid bin Zurayi told us, he said: Saeed told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, He said: “The fingers are ten, ten.”"
"6795","Ismail bin Masoud told us, he said: Khalid bin Al-Harith told us, he said: Husayn Al-Mu’allim told us, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, that His father told him, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, who said: When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, conquered Mecca, he said in his sermon: “And in “Ten fingers, ten.”"
"6796","Abdullah bin Al-Haytham told me, he said: Hajjaj told us, he said: Hammam told us, he said: Hussein Al-Mu’allim, and Ibn Jurayj told us, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said in his sermon, while leaning his back against The Kaaba: “The fingers are equal” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6797","Ismail bin Masoud told us, he said: Khalid bin Al-Harith told us, he said: Husayn Al-Mu’allim told us, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, that His father told him, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, who said: When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, conquered Mecca, he said in his sermon: “And in “The clarifiers are five by five.”"
"6798","Amr bin Mansour told us, he said: Al-Hakam bin Musa Abu Salih told us, he said: Yahya bin Hamza told us, on the authority of Suleiman bin Dawud said: Al-Zuhri told me, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Muhammad bin Amr bin Hazm, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings be upon him, wrote to the people of Yemen a book containing the duties, sunnahs, and blood money, and he sent it with Amr ibn Hazm, and it was read to The people of Yemen, and this is its copy: “From Muhammad the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, to Shurahbil bin Abdul Kalal, and Al-Harith bin Abdul Kalal, And Nu’aym ibn Abd Kulal, it was said: Dhu Ra’in, Maa’afir, and Hamadan, but later, and it was in his book: Whoever commits aggression against a believer, he will be killed for his sake. Clear evidence, for it is a sacrifice, unless the guardians of the murdered person are satisfied, and that the blood money for the soul is one hundred camels, and for the nose if its camel is loaded. Blood money, and blood money for the tongue, blood money for the lips, blood money for the two eggs, blood money for the penis, blood money for the back of the body, and blood money for the eyes. Blood money: half the blood money for a single leg, a third of the blood money for a female mother, a third of the blood money for a dead animal, and fifteen for a pregnant woman. Of camels, and on each finger of the hand and toe there are ten camels, and on the tooth there are five camels, and in the muddhah there are five camels, And the man should be killed with the woman, and the people of the religion must pay a thousand dinars.” Abu Abdul Rahman said: Muhammad bin Bakkar bin Bilal disagreed with him. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6799","Al-Haytham bin Marwan bin Al-Haytham bin Imran Al-Dimashqi informed us, saying: Muhammad bin Bakkar bin Bilal Al-Dimashqi told us, he said: Tell us Yahya bin Hamza, he said: Suleiman bin Arqam told us, he said: Al-Zuhri told me, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Muhammad bin Amr bin Hazm, On the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, wrote a letter to the people of Yemen, containing the duties, the sunnahs, and the blood money. And he sent it with Amr bin Hazm, and it was to be read to the people of Yemen. This was abrogated, so he mentioned something like it, except that he said: “And in the spring “One hand is half the blood money, half the blood money is given to one hand, and half the blood money is given to one foot.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: This is more like the truth, and God knows best, and Sulaiman bin Arqam is an abandoned hadith, and he narrated this hadith On the authority of Al-Zuhri, Yunus bin Yazid, mursal (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6800","Ahmad bin Amr bin Al-Sarh informed us, saying: Ibn Wahb told us, saying: Yunus bin Yazid informed me, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, he said: I read The letter of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, which he wrote to Amr ibn Hazm when he sent him to Najran, and the letter was with Abu Bakr ibn He was firm, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, wrote: “This is a statement from God and His Messenger: O you who have believed, fulfill the contracts.” So he wrote Verses from it, until he reached: Indeed, God is quick in reckoning, then he wrote: This is the book of wounds, in the soul is a hundred camels” and the like"
"6801","Ahmad bin Abd al-Wahid bin Aboud al-Dimashqi told us, he said: Marwan bin Muhammad told us, he said: Sa`id told us, on the authority of al-Zuhri, He said: Abu Bakr bin Hazm came to me with a letter on a piece of paper from Adam, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “This is a statement from God and His Messenger: O you who have believed, fulfill your contracts and recite verses from them. Then he said: In the soul is a hundred camels, and in the eye fifty, and in the hand fifty. And for a man fifty, and for a female mother a third of the blood money, and for a dead animal a third of the blood money, and for a movable animal fifteen obligatory, and for the fingers Ten is ten, and in the teeth there is five, and in the clearing there is five.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6802","Al-Harith bin Miskin, reading from him, on the authority of Ibn al-Qasim, he said: Malik told me, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Bakr bin Muhammad bin Amr ibn Hazm, on the authority of his father, said: The letter that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, wrote to Amr ibn Hazm, regarding the minds: “Indeed, in The soul is one hundred camels, and for the nose when a camel is loaded is a hundred camels, and for the motherhood is a third of the soul, and for the carcass the same, and in There are fifty for the eye, and fifty for the hand, and fifty for the foot, and for each finger there are ten camels, and for the tooth there are five, and for The explanation is five. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6803","Amr bin Mansour told us, he said: Muslim bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Aban told us, he said: Yahya told us, on the authority of Ishaq bin Abdullah bin Abi Talha, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, that a Bedouin came to the door of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and looked at the corner of the door. Then the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, hit him and stabbed him with an iron or a stick to gouge out his eye. When he saw, he was blinded, so the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said to him: He, peace be upon him, said: “If you had remained steadfast, I would have gouged out your eyes.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6804","Qutaibah bin Sa’id told us, he said: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, that Sahl bin Sa’d told him that a man came out of a burrow. In the chapter of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, a man scratching his head with it. When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saw him And he said: “If I had known that you were looking at me, I would have stabbed you in the eye with it. Indeed, the ear was created for the sake of sight.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6805","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, he said: Muadh bin Hisham told us, he said: My father told me, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Al-Nadr bin Anas, on the authority of Bashir bin Nahik, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Whoever enters a people’s house without their permission, and they same, there is no blood money, and there is no retaliation.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6806","Muhammad bin Mansour told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Abu al-Zinad, on the authority of al-Araj, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: “If someone were to look at you without permission, and you frightened him and gouged out his eyes, there would be no blame on you.” And he said again: Wing (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6807","Muhammad bin Musab Al-Sawri told us, he said: Muhammad bin Al-Mubarak told us, he said: Abdul-Aziz bin Muhammad told us, on the authority of Safwan bin Sulaym, on the authority of Ata’ ibn Yasar, on the authority of Abu Sa’id al-Khudri, that he was praying, and Ibn Marwan wanted to pass in front of him, so he turned him away. He did not come back, so he hit him, and the boy went out crying, until Marwan came and told him, and said: Marwan to Abu Saeed: Why did you hit your brother’s son? ? He said: I did not hit him, but I hit Satan. I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “If one of you was in his prayer, and he wanted to A person passes in front of him, and he repels him as much as he can, but if he refuses, then let him fight him, for he is a devil.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6808","Amr bin Uthman told me, he said: Al-Walid told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, he said: The Messenger said God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever seeks medicine, and no medicine was known of him before that, is liable.”"
"6809","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, he said: Abdul-Malik bin Abi Suleiman told us, he said: Saeed bin Jubayr told us, On the authority of Ibn Abbas, that Omar used to ask the immigrants about this verse: When God’s victory and conquest {1} come and you see the people, what was it revealed about? Some of them said: “God commanded His Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, when he saw people entering Islam and striving in religion, to praise God and seeks His forgiveness.” Omar said: “Am I not more impressed with you than Ibn Abbas? O Ibn Abbas, what is the matter with you that you do not speak?” He said: God taught him when he would die. He said: When God’s victory and conquest come {1} and you see people entering God’s religion in droves {2}, then this is your sign. From death, he said: You have spoken the truth, and by the One in Whose Hand is my soul, I did not know of it except what you knew. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6810","Muhammad bin Muammar told me, he said: Abu Dawud told us, he said: Abu Awanah told us, on the authority of Firas, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Masruq, he said Aisha told me, she said: We were with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and not one of us left. Then Fatima came walking, and not one of us left. By God, her walk was as bad as the walk of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, until she came to him and he said: “Welcome, my daughter.” So he made her sit. On his right, or on his left, then he made her do something, and she cried intensely. Then he made her do something, and she laughed. When the Messenger of God got up, May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. I said to her: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, singled you out among us with secrets, and are you crying? Tell me what he said to you? She said: I would not reveal his secret to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, died, I said to her: I ask you by the right that I have over you. What did the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, share with you? She said: But now, yes, he pleased me the first time. He said: Gabriel used to examine me with the Qur’an once every year, and he examined it with me twice a year, and I do not see the deadline unless it is drawing near, so fear God. And be patient, so I cried, then he said to me: O Fatima, are you not satisfied that you are the mistress of the women of this nation, or the mistress of the women of the worlds? I laughed? (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6811","Amr bin Hisham told me, he said: Muhammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, on the authority of Yaqoub bin Utba, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Abdullah, on the authority of Aisha, she said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, returned from a funeral, and I felt a headache in my head. And I say: And he headed it. He said: “Rather, I.” And he headed it. Then he said: It would not harm you if you died before me, so I washed you, shrouded you, and prayed. Then I buried you. I said: It would be as if I were yours if I did that. I returned to my house and had a wedding with some of your wives there. The Messenger smiled. May God bless him and grant him peace. Then he began to fall ill in which he died.” Muhammad ibn Ahmad disagreed with him, and he narrated it, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Salamah, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, on the authority of Yaqoub, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ubayd Allah ibn Abdullah, on the authority of Urwa (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6812","Abu Yusuf, the pharmacist, Al-Raqi Muhammad ibn Ahmad, told me from his book. He said: Muhammad ibn Salamah told us, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, on the authority of Yaqoub. On the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Abdullah bin Utbah, on the authority of Urwa bin Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Aisha, she said: A messenger returned to me. God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, one day after a funeral in Al-Baqi’, I was having a headache in my head, and I was saying: “And my head,” and he said: “Rather. “I am, Aisha.” He nodded, then said: By God, it would not harm you if you died before me. I washed you, shrouded you, and prayed upon you. Then I buried you. I said: It is as if I were with you, by God, if I had done that. I have returned to my house and married some of your wives there. The Messenger smiled. May God bless him and grant him peace. Then he began to suffer from the pain from which he died.” Salih bin Kaysan disagreed with him, and he narrated it, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6813","Abd al-Rahman bin Muhammad bin Salam al-Tarsusi reported, saying: Yazid bin Harun told us, saying: Ibrahim bin Saad told us, on the authority of Salih bin Kaysan, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered upon me on the day that began. So I said: And he headed it, and he said: “I wish that had happened while I was alive, so I prepared you and buried you, so I said differently: As if I were with you on that day.” A bride with some of your wives. He said: And he led him. Invite your father and your brother for me so that I may write a letter to Abu Bakr, for I fear that someone will say, He wishes for an interpretation, but God and the believers refuse except Abu Bakr.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6814","Muhammad bin Yahya bin Abdullah reported, saying: Abdul Razzaq told us, saying: Muammar reported, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa, and he told me Muawiyah bin Salih, he said: Yahya bin Ma’in told me, he said: Hisham bin Yusuf told us, on the authority of Muammar, he said: Al-Zuhri said: He informed me Urwah, on the authority of Aisha, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said in the pain in which he was seized: “Pour on me seven scabs that were not permissible.” I sent them to the table, so that I might know the people.” So we made him sit in Hafsa’s furnace, and we continued to pour water on him until he began to point to us. You did it. Abu Abdul Rahman said: Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak disagreed with them, and he narrated it, on the authority of Muammar, and Yunus, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Aisha (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6815","Suwayd bin Nasr bin Suwayd reported, saying: Abdullah reported on the authority of Muammar and Yunus, who said: Al-Zuhri said: Ubayd Allah bin Abdullah bin informed me Utba, that Aisha, the wife of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, became heavy and his pain became severe, He asked his wives for permission to nurse in my house, so he was given permission, so he went out between two men, his feet treading the ground, between Abbas and another man. Aisha said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said after he entered her house, and his pain became intense: “Throw on me seven unpeeled scabs.” I appointed them to the place, so that I might be well known to the people.” Aisha said: So we made him sit in the furnace of Hafsa, the wife of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and then We started pouring water on him from that close quarters, until he began to indicate to us with his hand, “You have done so.” She said: Then he went out to the people and led them in prayer. And he addressed them (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6816","Suwayd bin Nasr bin Suwayd reported, he said: Abdullah reported, on the authority of Zaida, he said: Musa bin Abi Aisha reported, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Abdullah, He said: I went to Aisha and said to her: Will you not tell me about the illness of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace? She said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, became heavy, so he said: “Did the people pray?” We said: No, they are waiting for you, O Messenger of God. He said: Put some water in it for me. The one who was dyed, so we did so, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, bathed, then he went to go to the water, and he fainted, then he woke up and said: Pray. The people? We said: No, they are waiting for you, O Messenger of God. She said: And the people are sitting in the mosque, waiting for the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. For the evening prayer, she said: So he sent a messenger to Abu Bakr to lead the people in prayer, so Abu Bakr, who was a gentle man, said: O Omar, pray With the people, Omar said to him: You have more right to that. He said: So Abu Bakr prayed in those days. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6817","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Yahya told us, he said: Sufyan told us, he said: Musa bin Abi Aisha told me, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Abd. By God, on the authority of Aisha, she said: We called the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, during his illness, and he said: “Do not give birth to me.” We said: The patient’s dislike of the medicine. When he woke up, he said: “None of you will remain except Ludd, except Al-Abbas, for he did not bear witness with you.”"
"6818","Ziyad bin Yahya Al-Basri told us, he said: Abdul Wahhab told us, he said: Ubayd Allah bin Omar told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, She said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, complained. He used to recite to himself exorcists and blow his nose. When his complaint became severe, I used to recite over him, and breathe out, and wipe over him with my hands, hoping for her blessing.”"
"6819","Ibrahim bin Muhammad al-Taymi reported, saying: Yahya told us, meaning Ibn Sa`id, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Sulayman, on the authority of Shaqiq, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Aisha, she said: “I have never seen pain for anyone more severe than it was for the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6820","Muhammad ibn Mansour reported, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, he said: Ubayd Allah informed me, he said: I asked Aisha about the illness of the Messenger of God. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, she said: “He complained, and he stopped blowing his nose, and we likened his blowing his nose to that of eating raisins, and he used to go around looking after his wives, so when The illness became severe. He asked them for permission to nurse with me and to visit him. They gave him permission, so he entered upon me while he was leaning on two legs, his legs crossed. There are two lines on the ground. One of them is Al-Abbas. I mentioned that to Ibn Abbas, and he said: Didn’t she tell you who the other was? I said: No. He said: He is Ali. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6821","Suwayd bin Nasr reported, saying: Abdullah, meaning Ibn al-Mubarak, reported on the authority of Muammar and Yunus, saying: Al-Zuhri said: Ubayd Allah bin Abdullah informed me By God, that Aisha and Abdullah bin Abbas said: When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, descended upon him, he began throwing his khamis on his face, and then He was saddened by her uncovering his face, and he said while doing so: “May the curse of God be upon the Jews and Christians, they have taken the graves of their prophets as places of worship.” He warns of what they did (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6822","Ubaid Allah bin Saad bin Ibrahim reported, he said: My uncle told us, he said: My father told us, on the authority of Salih, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, he said: Ubaid told me God bin Abdullah bin Utbah, that Aisha and Abdullah bin Abbas said: When it was revealed to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, he was overwhelmed He throws a khamisah on his face, and when he feels sad, he uncovers it from his face, and he says while doing so: “May the curse of God be upon the Jews and Christians. They took the graves of their prophets as places of worship.” He warns them of what they did. Abu Abdul Rahman said: This hadith was narrated by Ibrahim bin Saad, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Salih bin Kaysan, on the authority of Syphilis (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6823","Ubaid Allah bin Saad reported, he said: My uncle told us, he said: My father told us, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, he said: Salih bin Kaysan told me, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, On the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Abdullah bin Utbah, that Aisha and Ibn Abbas told him that, when the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came down And when he was sad, he revealed it from his face, and said while doing so: “May God’s curse be upon me.” The Jews and Christians took the graves of their prophets as places of worship.” Beware of his nation what they did, and this hadith was narrated by Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab L3299, on the authority of Abu Hurairah (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6824","Amr ibn Sawad ibn al-Aswad ibn Amr reported, on the authority of Ibn Wahb, who said: Malik reported, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Sa`id ibn al-Musayyab, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “God has fought the Jews, for they have taken the graves of their prophets as places of worship.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Qatada disagreed with him, so he narrated it, on the authority of Sa`id bin al-Musayyab, on the authority of Aisha. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6825","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Khalid bin Al-Harith told us, he said: Saeed told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Aisha, on the authority of The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “May God curse a people who take the graves of their prophets as places of worship.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6826","Ahmad bin Sulaiman Al-Rahawi reported, saying: Abu Dawud Al-Hafari told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Sulayman Al-Taymi, on the authority of Anas, he said: The Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he will command upon his death: “Prayer and what your right hands possess.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Sulayman al-Taymi did not hear this hadith from Anas. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6827","Ishaq bin Ibrahim reported, on the authority of Jarir, on the authority of Suleiman, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Anas, who said: It was generally the will of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: “Prayer and what your right hands possess.” It was narrated by Al-Mu`tamir bin Sulaiman Al-Taymi, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of a companion of his, on the authority of Anas, Hilal bin Al-Ala told me, he said: Al-Khattabi told us, he said: Al-Mu’tamir told us, he said: I heard my father, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of a friend of his, on the authority of Anas. . . Similar to it, Abu Awanah disagreed with it, and he narrated it, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of a ship"
"6828","Qutaibah bin Saeed reported, saying: Abu Awanah told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of the ship of the slave of Umm Salamah, he said: He was generally the will of the Messenger of God. God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Prayer and what your right hands possess,” so he began repeating it until it stirred in his chest and what was overflowing. It was narrated by Saeed bin Abi Arouba, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Safina, on the authority of Umm Salamah."
"6829","Humayd ibn Masada reported, he said: Yazid told us, he said: Sa`id told us, on the authority of Qatada, that the ship of the slave of Umm Salamah was narrated, on the authority of Umm Salamah. She said: The general will of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, upon his death was: “Prayer and what your right hands possess,” until he made it stab at his chest. And his tongue does not overflow with it. Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Qatada did not hear it from a ship. Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak reported, he said: Yunus told us, he said: Shayban told us, on the authority of Qatada, he said: he told us about a ship The servant of Umm Salamah, because he used to say: It was generally the will of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. . . A similar hadith was narrated by Hammam, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Abu al-Khalil, on the authority of a ship (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6830","Abd al-Rahman bin Muhammad bin Salam reported, saying: Yazid told us, he said: Hammam told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Abu al-Khalil, on the authority of a ship, On the authority of Umm Salamah, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, while he was dying, began to say: “Prayer and what your right hands possess,” so he began to say it and then continue. Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Abu al-Khalil’s name is Saleh bin Abi Maryam. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6831","Suleiman bin Dawud reported, he said: Ibn Wahb reported, he said: Al-Layth informed me, on the authority of Ibn Al-Haad, on the authority of Musa bin Sarjis, on the authority of Al-Qasim, on the authority of Aisha said: I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, as he was dying, and he had a cup of water in it. He put his hand into the cup and wiped it. His face with water, then he says: “Oh God, help me in the throes of death.”"
"6832","Muhammad bin Wahb Al-Harrani told me, he said: Muhammad bin Salamah told us, he said: Ibn Ishaq told me, he said: Ya’qub bin Utba told me On the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, she said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, returned that day and lay on my lap. Then a man from the family of Abu Bakr entered upon me, with a green siwak in his hand. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, looked at me and I knew he wanted it. I said: “O Messenger of God, would you like me to give you this siwak siwak?” He said: Yes, she said: So I took it, softened it, then gave it to him, and he used it as tightly as I had ever seen him. He used a siwak before, then He put it down, and I found the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, weighing heavily on my lap, so I went to look at his face, and lo and behold, his sight had cleared. And he says: “Rather, the companion is higher than Paradise.” I said: You were given a choice and you chose, by the One who sent you with the truth. She said: And the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was arrested. He said hello (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6833","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak reported, saying: Waki` told us, on the authority of Shu`bah, on the authority of Sa`d bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha: I had heard that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, would not die until he had a choice between this world and the hereafter, so his illness took hold of him. On which he died, I heard him saying: “Among those whom You have bestowed of the prophets, the truthful, the martyrs, and the righteous, and the good of those are “Friend,” so I thought he was good (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6834","Muhammad bin Ali bin Maymun Al-Raqqi told me, Al-Faryabi told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khalid, on the authority of Abu Burdah, On the authority of Aisha, she said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, fainted while he was in my lap, so I started wiping him and praying for his recovery, and he woke up. He said: “Rather, I ask God for the highest companion, the happiest, with Gabriel, Michael, and Israfil.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6835","Ishaq bin Ibrahim reported, he said: Abdah reported, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Abbad bin Abdullah bin Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Aisha, she said: I heard The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said upon his death: “O God, forgive me, have mercy on me, and join me with the highest companion.”"
"6836","Amr bin Mansour reported, he said: Abdullah bin Yusuf told us, he said: Al-Layth told us, he said: Ibn al-Haad told me, on the authority of Abdul Rahman Ibn Al-Qasim, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, died, and he was in the sight of my throat and my taster, and I did not “I hate the severity of death for anyone, after what I saw from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.”"
"6837","Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Ayyub ibn Ibrahim al-Marwazi informed us, saying: Mahrez ibn al-Wadah narrated to us, saying: Ismail ibn Umayyah narrated to us. On the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Anas, he said: “The last time I looked at the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he complained, so he ordered Abu Bakr to pray.” With the people, while we were in the noon prayer, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, uncovered Aisha’s room with his hand, and looked at the people. I looked at “His face is as if it were a leaf of the Qur’an.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6838","Muhammad ibn Qudamah reported, saying: Jarir told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Umm Musa, she said: Umm Salamah said: And what Umm Salamah swears by is, The closest person to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was Ali. She said: The day after the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was arrested, he sent The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, went to him, and it was as if I saw that he had sent for a need. I thought he had sent him, so he started saying: “Ali came? Three times, so he came before The sun rose, and when he came, we knew that he had a need, so we left the house, and we were visiting the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. On that day, in Aisha’s house, I was the last to leave the house. Then I sat near the door to them, and Ali leaned on him, and he was the last. people with him as a covenant, he made his way and conversed with him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6839","Qutaibah bin Saeed reported, saying: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Anas, who said: “The last look I looked at the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings be upon him, opened the curtain, and the people were in rows behind Abu Bakr. Abu Bakr wanted to apostatize, so he motioned to them to stay, and he threw Al-Sajf, and he died at the end of that day, which was a Monday."
"6840","Abu Al-Tahir reported to Ahmad bin Amr bin Al-Sarh, he said: Ibn Wahb told us, he said: Yunus told me, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Urwa, On the authority of Aisha: Abu Bakr “kissed the eyes of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, while he was dead.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6841","Yaqoub bin Ibrahim reported, he said: Yahya told us, on the authority of Sufyan, he said: Musa bin Abi Aisha told me, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Abdullah. On the authority of Ibn Abbas and on the authority of Aisha: that Abu Bakr “kissed the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, while he was dead.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6842","Suleiman bin Saif reported, saying: Ya’qub told us, he said: My father told us, on the authority of Salih, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, that Abu Salama told him, on the authority of Aisha, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was imprisoned when he died in a piece of dotted clothing.”"
"6843","Muhammad bin Khalaf Al-Asqalani reported, he said: Adam told us, he said: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Aqeel, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha. She said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, died when he was sixty-three years old.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6844","Abd al-Rahman ibn Ubayd Allah al-Halabi reported, on the authority of Ibn Abi Zaydah, on the authority of Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq, on the authority of al-Sha`bi, on the authority of Jarir, who said: We were With Muawiyah, he said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was arrested when he was sixty-three.”"
"6845","Qutaibah bin Saeed reported, saying: Hafs told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was shrouded. He was greeted in three white Yemeni dresses, a robe, without a shirt or turban. He said: Then he mentioned to Aisha their saying: In two clothes and a cloak. She said: “He was brought in a hail, but they returned it and did not shroud him in it.”"
"6846","Abu Dawud reported, he said: Ya’qub told us, he said: My father told us, on the authority of Salih, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, that Abu Salama told him about Aisha, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was imprisoned when he died in a piece of dotted clothing.”"
"6847","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna reported, on the authority of Al-Walid, he said: Al-Awza’i narrated to us, and Mujahid bin Musa reported, saying: Al-Walid bin Muslim narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i. He said: Al-Zuhri narrated to me, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Muhammad, on the authority of Aisha, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, had an ink streaked on his garment. Then it was delayed.” The wording is by Ibn al-Muthanna (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6848","Qutaybah ibn Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Humayd ibn 'Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Salamah ibn Nabt, from Nu'aym, from Nabt, from Salim ibn 'Ubayd, who said — and he was one of the Companions of the Suffah: ""The Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, fell unconscious during his illness. Then he regained consciousness and said: 'Has the prayer come in?' They said: 'Yes.' He said: 'Command Bilal to give the adhan, and command Abu Bakr to lead the people in prayer.' Then he fell unconscious again. He regained consciousness and said: 'Has the prayer come in?' We said: 'Yes.' He said: 'Command Bilal to give the adhan, and command Abu Bakr to lead the people in prayer.' 'A'ishah said: 'My father is a tender-hearted man.' He said: 'You are among the companions of Yusuf. Command Bilal to give the adhan, and command Abu Bakr to lead the people in prayer.' So they commanded Bilal to give the adhan, and they commanded Abu Bakr to lead the people in prayer. When the prayer was commenced, the Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, said: 'Has the prayer been commenced?' We said: 'Yes.' He said: 'Bring me a person on whom I may lean.' So Barirah came, and another person with her. He leaned upon her and came, while Abu Bakr was praying. He sat beside him. Abu Bakr began to move back, but he held him until he finished the prayer."" He said: ""When the Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, passed away, 'Umar said: 'Let no one speak of his death, or I shall strike him with this sword of mine.' So they fell silent. They were an unlettered people among whom there had been no prophet before him. They said: 'O Salim, go to the companion of the Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, and call him.' He said: 'I went out and found Abu Bakr standing in the mosque.' Abu Bakr said: 'The Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, has died.' I said: ''Umar says: ""Let no one speak of his death, or I shall strike him with this sword of mine.""' He placed his hand upon his forearm, then he set out walking until he entered. He said: 'They made room for him until he came to the Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, and bent over him, until his face nearly touched the face of the Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, until it became clear to him that he had indeed died.' Abu Bakr said: 'You are mortal, and they are mortal.' They said: 'O companion of the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, has the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, died?' He said: 'Yes.' He said: 'They knew that he had spoken the truth.' They said: 'O companion of the Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, shall the Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, be prayed over?' He said: 'Yes.' They said: 'How shall we pray over him?' He said: 'Groups shall enter and make takbir and supplicate, then they shall leave and others shall come.' They said: 'O companion of the Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, shall the Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, be buried?' He said: 'Yes.' They said: 'Where shall he be buried?' He said: 'In the place where Allah took his soul, for He did not take his soul except in a pure place.' He said: 'They knew that he had spoken the truth.' Then Abu Bakr said: 'Your companion is with you.' Abu Bakr went out, and the Muhajirun gathered and began to consult among themselves. Then they said: 'Go to our brothers among the Ansar, for they have a share in this right.' They came to the Ansar, and the Ansar said: 'An amir from us and an amir from you.' 'Umar said: 'Two swords in one sheath — they cannot be reconciled.' Then he took the hand of Abu Bakr and said: 'Who has these three verses: ""When he said to his companion"" — who is his companion? ""When they were both in the grotto"" — who were they? ""Grieve not, for Allah is with us"" — with whom?' Then he gave him the bay'ah. Then he said: 'Give the bay'ah.' So the people gave the best and most beautiful pledge of allegiance."""
"6849","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Abdul Rahman told us, he said: Abdullah bin Jafar told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Muhammad bin Saad, on the authority of his father On the authority of Saad, he said: “Accuse me of being an atheist, and camp against me, as was done to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6850","Harun bin Abdullah reported, saying: Abu Amer told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Jaafar, on the authority of Ismail bin Muhammad bin Saad, on the authority of Amer Ibn Sa’d, on the authority of Sa’d, said: “Punish my punishment, and set up an ambush against me, as was done to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6851","Qutaibah bin Saeed reported, saying: Humaid bin Abdul Rahman told us, on the authority of Salamah bin Nabit, on the authority of Nu’aym, on the authority of Nabit, on the authority of Salim bin Ubaid, he said: “When the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, died, they said: O Salem, go to the companion of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and invite him. So I went out and found Abu Bakr standing in the mosque. He said: He put his hand on my forearms, then he began walking until he entered, and they made room for him until He came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and fell upon him until it became clear to him that he had died, so Abu Bakr said: You are dead and they are dead. They said: O companion of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. Will the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, be buried? He said: Yes. They said: Where will he be buried? He said: In the place? In which God took his soul, for he only took his soul in a good place. He said: So they knew that it was as he said. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6852","Ismail bin Masoud Al-Jahdari reported on the authority of Yazid, who was Ibn Zurai’, who said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Abu Jamrah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, He said: “A red velvet was placed under the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, when he was buried.”"
"6853","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Jarir told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Abu Wael, on the authority of Amr bin Shurahbil, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: I asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “Which sin is the greatest in the sight of God?” He said: “To make a rival to God while He created you.” I said: That is Great, I said: Then what? He said: Then you kill your son, fearing that he will share with you. I said: Then what? He said: To commit adultery with your neighbor’s girlfriend."
"6854","Abdul Rahman bin Muhammad bin Salam told us, he said: Abu Samah told us, on the authority of Malik bin Mughul, he said: I heard Wasil bin Hayyan, he mentioned On the authority of Abu Wael, he said: Abdullah said: I asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, I said: O Messenger of God, “Which sin is greater?” He said: To make you a rival to God, and He created you. I said: Then what? He said: To kill your son so that he may eat with you. I said: Then what? He said: Then? “You commit adultery with your neighbour’s consort.” Then he read this verse: “And those who do not call upon another god with God,” until His saying: “He casts upon sins.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6855","Humaid bin Mukhlid Al-Nasa’i told me, he said: Muhammad bin Yusuf told us, he said: Al-Awza’i told us, he said: Al-Zuhri told me, on the authority of Abu Salamah bin Abd The Most Gracious, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The adulterer does not commit adultery when he commits adultery while he is a believer, and the thief does not steal when he is a believer.” He steals while he is a believer, he does not drink alcohol when he drinks it while he is a believer, and he does not plunder a place of honor by which believers are exalted to him. Their sight, but when it is stolen by a believer.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6856","Ishaq bin Mansour Al-Maruzi told us, he said: Abu Al-Mughirah told us, and Imran bin Bakkar Al-Barrad told me, he said: Abu Al-Barrad told us. Al-Mughirah, and the pronunciation is by Imran. He said: Al-Awza’i narrated to us, he said: Al-Zuhri narrated to me, on the authority of Sa’id, and Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: “The adulterer does not commit adultery when he commits adultery while he is a believer, and the thief does not steal when he steals while he is a believer, and he does not drink alcohol.” And when a believer drinks it, and does not take it as an honorable plunder, the believers will raise their eyes to him. \ (Peace Be Upon Him)"""""
"6857","Ishaq bin Mansour and Muhammad bin Yahya bin Abdullah Al-Naysaburi told us, and the wording is his, on the authority of Muhammad bin Kathir, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Humaid bin Abdul Rahman, Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, and Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: He said The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “An adulterer does not commit adultery when a believer is committing adultery, and a thief does not commit adultery when a believer is committing theft, nor does he drink.” “Alcohol is when a believer drinks it, and it is not plundered, people raise their eyes. It is when a believer drinks it, and it is not plundered.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6858","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: I am Al-Walid bin Muslim, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, he said: Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab and Abu Salama bin Abdul Rahman, and Abu Bakr bin Abdul Rahman, all of them told me, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, He said: “The adulterer does not commit adultery when he commits adultery while he is a believer, and the thief does not steal when he steals while he is a believer, and he does not drink alcohol when he drinks it while he is a believer.” A believer, and he does not plunder a piece of honor to which Muslims raise their eyes, and when he plunders it he is a believer.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6859","Al-Abbas bin Al-Walid bin Mazyd Al-Beiruti told us, he said: My father told me, he said: Al-Awza’i told us, he said: Al-Zuhri told me, he said: Abu Salamah, Sa`id, and Abu Bakr told me, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The adulterer does not commit adultery while he is When a believer commits adultery, and the thief does not steal when a believer steals, and he does not drink alcohol when a believer drinks it, and he does not loot. It is of honor to which believers raise their gazes, and it is when a believer seizes it.”"
"6860","Issa bin Hammad bin Zugha told us, he said: I am Al-Layth, on the authority of Aqeel, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The adulterer does not commit adultery when he commits adultery while he is a believer, and the one who drinks it does not drink wine when he commits adultery.” He drinks it while he is a believer, and the thief does not steal when he is a believer, and he does not plunder such a thing that people raise their eyes to him when he He seizes it, and he is a believer.” Issa bin Hammad told us, he said: I am Al-Layth, on the authority of Aqeel, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Saeed, and Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Messenger God, may God bless him and grant him peace, like this hadith of Abu Bakr, except for looting."
"6861","Isma bin Al-Fadl Al-Naysaburi told me, he said: Harami bin Amara told me, he said: I am Shu’bah, on the authority of Amara bin Abi Hafsa, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, said: “The fornicator does not commit adultery when he commits adultery while he is a believer, and he does not steal when he steals while he is a believer, and he does not drink alcohol.” When he drinks it while he is a believer.”"
"6862","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Al-Junaid Abu Abdullah Al-Hijjam told us, he said: Zayd, the cupper, told us, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The adulterer does not commit adultery while he is a believer, and the thief does not steal while he is a believer, and he does not drink alcohol.” And he is a believer.”"
"6863","Abd al-Rahman bin Muhammad bin Salam told us, he said: Ishaq al-Azraq told us, on the authority of al-Fudayl bin Ghazwan, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “A servant does not commit adultery while he is a believer, and he does not drink alcohol when he drinks it while he is a believer.” A believer, and he does not steal while he is a believer, and he does not kill while he is a believer.” So I said to Ibn Abbas: How was faith taken away from him? He interlaced his fingers, then took them out. He said: This is how, and when he repents, he will return to it like this, and interlace his fingers. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6864","Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Maymun al-Ruqi told us, he said: Muhammad is the son of Yusuf told us, he said: Sufyan is al-Thawri told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Rabi’i bin Harash, on the authority of Abu Dharr, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “God loves three, and hates three. “The arrogant and insignificant person, the miserly and arrogant person, and the adulterous old man.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6865","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, he said: Muhammad told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Mansour, he said: I heard Ruba’i, speaking, on the authority of Zaid bin Dhabyan, who transmitted it to Abu Dharr, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: “There are three whom God loves, and three whom God hates. The three Those whom God hates: the adulterous old man, the deceitful poor man, and the unjust rich man. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6866","Muhammad ibn al-Ala al-Kufi informed us, saying: Abu Muawiyah narrated to us on the authority of al-Amash, and Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad ibn Salam informed us, saying: Muhammad narrated to us Ibn Rabi’ah, who said: Al-A’mash told us, on the authority of Abu Hazim, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “There are three that God does not wait for.” On the Day of Resurrection, he will not purify them, and for them will be a painful punishment: the adulterous old man, the false imam, and the deceitful breadwinner.” Muhammad bin Al-Ala said in his hadith: An adulterous sheikh, a lying king, and an arrogant breadwinner. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6867","Abu Dawud Al-Harrani told us, he said: A`rim told us, he said: Hammad, who is Ibn Zayd, told us, he said: Ubayd Allah bin Umar told us, on the authority of Sa`id bin Abi Saeed Al-Maqbari, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “There are four whom God hates: the seller who swears an oath, And the deceitful poor man, and the adulterous old man, and the unjust imam.”"
"6868","Amr ibn Yazid al-Basri informed us, he said: Bahz narrated to us, he said: Shu`bah narrated to us, on the authority of Salamah ibn Kuhayl, on the authority of al-Shu`bi, that Ali was flogged He slaughtered her on Thursday, and stoned her on Friday. He said: “I flogged you according to the Book of God, and I stoned you according to the Sunnah of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.”"
"6869","Muhammad bin Ismail bin Ibrahim bin Aliya told us, he said: Wahb is Ibn Jarir told us, he said: I am Shu’bah, on the authority of Salamah bin Kuhail And Mujalid, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Ali: He beat Sharaha on the Thursday, and stoned her on the Friday, and said: “I will flog you according to the Book of God.” And I stone you according to the Sunnah of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6870","Ahmad ibn Harb al-Mawsili informed us, saying: Qasim, who is ibn Yazid, told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Hattan ibn Abdullah, on the authority of Ubadah, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Take it from me. God has made a way for them. A hundred, stoning with stones, a virgin for a virgin, a hundred lashes, and banishment for a year.”"
"6871","Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Yazid told us, and he is Ibn Zuray’, he said: Sa’id told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Hattan bin Abdullah Al-Raqqashi, on the authority of Ubadah ibn Al-Samit, said: Whenever it was revealed to him, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was distressed and dismayed. His face, so it came down to him one day, and he met that, and when it was hidden from him, he said: “Take it from me, God has made a way for them, the virgin “For a virgin, one hundred lashes and exile for a year, and a married man for a married man, one hundred lashes, and stoning.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6872","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Hushaym told us, on the authority of Mansour bin Zazan, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Hattan bin Abdullah, on the authority of Ubadah Ibn al-Samit said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Take it from me. God has made a way for them, one garment for another, a hundred lashes. And stoning, and the virgin for the virgin, a hundred lashes, and exile for a year.”"
"6873","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna informed us, he said: Muhammad told us, he said: Shu`bah told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Yunus ibn Jubayr, on the authority of Kathir ibn al-Salt, he said: Zaid bin Thabit said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “When an old man or a young woman commits adultery, stone them absolutely.” Omar said: When it was revealed, I came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: Write it down. Shu’bah said: It is as if he disliked that. Omar said: Don’t you see that if an old man is not married, he is flogged, and that if a young man commits adultery while being married, he is stoned? (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6874","Ahmad ibn Amr ibn al-Sarh informed us in his hadith, on the authority of Ibn Wahb, he said: Al-Layth ibn Sa’d informed me, on the authority of Sa’id ibn Abi Hilal, On the authority of Marwan bin Uthman, on the authority of Abu Umamah bin Sahl, that his maternal aunt told him, saying: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, taught us it. He mentioned the verse about stoning: “The old man and the old woman, stone them absolutely for what they have spent of pleasure.”"
"6875","Ibrahim bin Yaqoub Al-Jawzjani told me, he said: Ibn Abi Maryam told us, he said: I am Al-Layth, he said: Khaled bin Yazid told me, on the authority of Saeed bin Abi Hilal, on the authority of Marwan bin Othman, on the authority of Abu Umamah bin Sahl, he said: My aunt told me, she said: The Messenger of God read to us God, may God bless him and grant him peace, the verse of stoning: “The old man and the old woman, stone them absolutely for what they have spent of pleasure.”"
"6876","Ismail bin Masoud Al-Jahdari told us, he said: Khalid bin Al-Harith told us, he said: Ibn Aoun told us, on the authority of Muhammad, he said: I was informed on the authority of Ibn My brother Kathir ibn al-Salt said: We were with Marwan, and among us was Zaid ibn Thabit. Zaid said: We used to recite: “The old man and the old woman, so stone them.” “At all.” Marwan said: Will you not put it in the Qur’an? He said: He said: Don't you see that the two young men are being stoned? We mentioned that and Omar was among us, so he said: I will heal you. We said: How is that? He said: I will go to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, God willing, and mention such-and-such, and when he mentions the verse of stoning, I will say: O Messenger of God, write for me the verse of stoning. He said: So he came to him, so he mentioned that to him. He mentioned the verse of stoning, and he said: O Messenger of God, Write for me the verse about stoning. He said: “I cannot.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6877","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, he said: Muhammad bin Jafar told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Ezra, on the authority of Al-Hasan Al-Arni, on the authority of Ubaid bin Nudhaylah, on the authority of Masruq, said: Ubayy bin Ka’b said: “They are flogged and stoned, and they are stoned but not flogged, and they are flogged and not They will be stoned. Qatada interpreted it as: The married old man, if he commits adultery, will be flogged and then stoned. The married young man will be stoned if he commits adultery, and the young man who commits adultery will be stoned. If he is not guarded, he will be flogged (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6878","Muawiyah bin Salih Al-Ash’ari informed me. He said: Mansour told us, he is Ibn Abi Muzahim. He said: Abu Hafs told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Asim. On the authority of Zirr, he said: Ubayy ibn Ka’b said: “How many verses do you count as Surah Al-Ahzab?” We said: Seventy-three, so Ubayy said: It would be equivalent to Surah Al-Ahzab. Al-Baqarah, and indeed it contains a verse about stoning: The old man and the old woman, then stone them absolutely as a punishment from Allah, and Allah is Mighty, All-Wise."
"6879","Al-Abbas bin Muhammad Al-Duri told us, he said: Abu Nuh Abdul-Rahman bin Ghazwan told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Saad bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Abdullah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Awf, he said: Omar addressed us, and he said: I have known that people They say: “The caliphate of Abu Bakr was a fluke, but God protected it from its evil, and there is no caliphate except through consultation, and any man who pledges allegiance to another Without consultation, neither of them should be ordered to be killed unannounced. Shu’bah said: I said to Saad: Why should they be killed? He said: Their punishment is not One of them is commanded, and they say: By stoning! The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, stoned us, and God revealed in His Book, had it not been People say: It was added in the Book of God, so I would have written it in my own handwriting, until I added it to the Book. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6880","Harun bin Abdullah al-Hammal told me, he said: Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Saad bin Ibrahim, he said: I heard Ubayd Allah bin Abdullah bin Utbah, speaking, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Awf. He said: Omar proposed a speech, and he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “was stoned, and we were stoned after him.”"
"6881","Muhammad bin Rafi’ al-Naysaburi told us, he said: Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Saad bin Ibrahim, he said: I heard Ubayd Allah bin Abdullah bin Utbah narrates, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that Omar bin Al-Khattab wanted to get engaged in Mina, so he informed Therein, Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf said to him: Only a mob of people is attending you here, so if you delay that until you advance to Medina, So he delayed it until he came to Medina, and said: So I approached the pulpit, and I heard him delivering a sermon, and he said in his sermon: Indeed, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “He was stoned, and we stoned after him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6882","Al-Hasan bin Ismail bin Suleiman Al-Mujalidi told me, he said: Hajjaj bin Muhammad told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Saad bin Ibrahim, he said: I heard Ubayd Allah bin Abdullah, speaking, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Awf, who said: Omar performed Hajj and wanted to get engaged. He addressed the people, and Abd al-Rahman bin Awf said to him: The rabble and the lowly of the people have gathered with you, so delay that until you come. Medina, he said: When he came to Medina, I approached the pulpit, and I heard him say: “I have known people who say: The caliphate of my father Bakr was a blunder, and God protected her from evil. There is no caliphate except by consultation, so neither of them should be ordered to kill people They say: What is the matter with stoning, when only in the Book of God is flogging! The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, stoned us after him, had it not been for They say: “I confirmed in the Book of God what is not in it, so I would confirm it as it was revealed.” Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Adhrami told me, he said: Ghandar told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Saad bin Ibrahim, he said: I heard Ubaid Allah bin Abdullah bin Utbah narrates, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Awf, who said: Omar bin Al-Khattab’s Hajj, So he wanted to address the people, and Abdul Rahman said: The crowd of people had gathered, so he delayed that. . . Towards him (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6883","Muhammad bin Mansour Al-Makki told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Abdullah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: I heard Omar say: I feared that the time of the people would pass for a long time, until someone said: We do not find stoning in the Book of God, for they would go astray by neglecting an obligatory duty. God sent it down, saying that stoning is due on the one who commits adultery if he is married, and there is clear evidence, or there is a pregnancy, or a confession, and it has been We read it: “When an old man or a woman commits adultery, stone them absolutely.” The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, stoned them. \After him.\"" Abu Abd al-Rahman said: I do not know that anyone mentioned in this hadith: The old man and the old woman"
"6884","Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Naysaburi told us, he said: Bishr ibn Umar told us, he said: Malik told me, on the authority of al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ubayd Allah ibn Abd God, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that Omar said: “Indeed, God sent Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, and sent down the Book to him, and he was in what was revealed to him.” The verse about stoning, so we read it and understood it, “And the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, stoned us,” and we stoned after him, and I fear that the people will remain for a long time. For someone to say: We do not find a verse about stoning in the Book of God, so he abandons a duty that God has sent down, and that stoning in the Book of God is a duty upon one who commits adultery. If he is chaste among men and women, if there is evidence against him, or there is a pregnancy, or a confession (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6885","Al-Harith bin Miskin, reading from him, and I hear, on the authority of Ibn Wahb, he said: Malik told me, and Yunus, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, he said: Ubaid Allah bin Abdullah told me that he heard Abdullah bin Abbas say: Omar said while he was sitting on the pulpit of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Peace and blessings of God be upon him: Indeed, God sent, meaning, Muhammad, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, with the truth, and sent down the Book to him, and it was while He revealed to him the verse of stoning We read it, we understood it, and we understood it, “And the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was stoned,” and we stoned him after him, so I fear that he will harm the people. A long time ago, someone would say: By God, we do not find stoning in the Book of God, so they would go astray by abandoning an obligation that God has revealed, and that stoning in the Book of God is a right. On the one who commits adultery if he is married, whether men or women, if evidence is established, or there is pregnancy, or there is a confession. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6886","Ubaid Allah bin Saad bin Ibrahim bin Saad told us, he said: My uncle told us, he said: My father told us, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, he said: Abdullah told me Bin Abi Bakr bin Muhammad bin Amr bin Hazm, on the authority of Muhammad bin Muslim Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Abdullah bin Utba, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abbas, he said: Omar addressed the people on the pulpit, and he said: What God willed him to say, then he said: God has sent, meaning, Muhammad May God’s prayers and peace be upon him in truth, and He sent down the Book to him, and among the verses of stoning that was revealed to him was the verse of stoning, so we read it, understood it, and understood it. And the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was stoned, and we stoned after him. I fear that if the people remain for a long period of time, someone will say: By God, we will not find anything. Stoning is in the Book of God, so they go astray by abandoning a duty that God has sent down, and stoning in the Book of God is a duty upon one who commits adultery if he is married among men. And women, if there is evidence, or pregnancy, or confession. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6887","Yusuf bin Saeed bin Muslim Al-Masisi told us, he said: Hajjaj bin Muhammad told us, he said: Laith bin Saad told us, on the authority of Aqeel, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, On the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Abdullah, that Ibn Abbas told him that he used to recite Abd al-Rahman bin Awf, and that Abd al-Rahman bin One day, Awf returned to him from Omar, during the last Hajj that Omar performed while he was in Mina. Abdul Rahman bin Awf said to Abdullah bin Abbas: If you saw a man who had just come to Omar and told him that a man said: By God, if Omar died, I would have pledged allegiance to so-and-so. Omar said: I will stand by the evening. God willing, then warn them about this group of people who usurp them. Abdul Rahman said: So I said: O Commander of the Faithful, do not do that. This is your day, for the season brings together a crowd of people, so I fear that you will say something that they fly every bird with, and they do not put it on Its location is given more time until you reach Medina, for it is the home of migration, the Sunnah, and faith, so you will be saved by the people’s jurists and nobles, she says. You did not say you were able, so they will understand your statement and put it in its proper place. Omar said: If I bring a righteous person to Medina, I will speak to the people about it. In the first place I will stand, God willing, Ibn Abbas said: When I came to Medina, I migrated to Friday, and I found Saeed bin Zaid who had preceded me. Al-Tahjri, so he sat next to the pulpit, and I sat next to him, but Omar did not want to leave, so he sat on the pulpit, and he recited the tashahhud, so he praised On God for what He deserves, then he said: As for what follows, I am telling you something, I do not know, perhaps it will be in my hands for my time, so whoever has understood it and is aware of it, Let him tell it wherever his mount ends, and whoever fears that he will not understand it, then it is not permissible for anyone to lie to me: Indeed, God has sent Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace. And the Book was sent down to him, and what was revealed to him was: the verse of stoning. So we recited it, “And the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, stoned “And we stoned after him, so I fear that if the people remain for a long period of time, someone will say: We do not find stoning in the Book of God, so they will go astray by abandoning it.” An obligation sent down by God, and stoning in the Book of God is a duty upon anyone who commits adultery, if he is chaste, whether men or women, if there is evidence, or It was the rope, or the confession (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6888","Ali bin Othman Al-Harrani told us, he said: Muhammad bin Musa told us, he said: Ubayy told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Ayyub, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Habib, On the authority of a man, on the authority of Saeed bin Abi Hind, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Abdullah bin Utbah bin Masoud, who said: Omar said on the pulpit: “I have The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was stoned.” And we stoned (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6889","Muhammad bin Aqeel Al-Naysaburi told us, he said: I am Ali bin Al-Hussein, he said: my father told me, he said: Yazid the grammarian told me, he said: he told me Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, said: “Whoever disbelieves in stoning has disbelieved in the Qur’an in a way that he did not expect. His saying: O People of the Book Our Messenger has come to you explaining to you much of what you concealed from the Scripture, so stoning occurred for what they concealed. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6890","Ibrahim bin Yaqoub Al-Jawzjani told me, he said: Yahya bin Ya’la bin Al-Harith told us, he said: Ubayy told us, he said: Ghaylan bin Jami’ told us, On the authority of Alqamah ibn Marthad, on the authority of Sulayman ibn Buraydah, on the authority of his father, he said: Ma’iz ibn Malik came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: O Messenger of God, purify me. He said: “Woe to you! Go back, ask forgiveness from God, and repent to Him.” He returned not far away, then came to him and said: O Messenger of God. God, purify me. Then the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said the same thing, until it was the fourth time. Then the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said to him: Why? Shall I cleanse you? He said: From adultery. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, asked: Is he mad? He was informed that he was not mad. He asked: Did you drink wine? So he stood up A man smelled it, but he did not smell any smell of wine. Then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Are you Atheeb? He said: Yes, so he ordered that he be stoned So the people were divided into two groups. Someone said: A goat perished for his worst deed. His sin surrounded him. And someone said: Repentance. Better than the repentance of Ma’iz ibn Malik, he came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he put his hand in his and said: Kill me. With stones? So they stayed like that for two or three days, then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, came while they were sitting, so he greeted, then sat down and said: They asked forgiveness for Ma'iz ibn Malik, and they said: May God forgive Ma'iz ibn Malik, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: He has repented with complete repentance, if only Divided among a hundred, it would have enlarged them.” Abu Abd al-Rahman told us: This is a valid chain of narration. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6891","Al-Abbas bin Abdul-Azeem Al-Anbari told us, on the authority of Al-Dahhak bin Mukhlid, he said: I am Ibn Jurayj, he said: I am Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of a cousin Abu Hurairah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: A goat came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: I have committed adultery, so he turned away from it, until It was on the fifth day that he came to him and said: “You married her until there was no longer that from you, is that part of her?” He said: Yes, he said: Just as what is absent in He said: Yes, he said: Do you know what fornication is? He said: Did you commit something forbidden from her, just as a man does? His wife is lawful. He said: What do you want? He said: I want you to purify me. So he ordered him to be stoned, so he was stoned. Then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, heard two men. Two of his companions said: Look at this one you are covering, then his soul did not calm down until he was stoned like the stones of a dog, and he mentioned a word that means: so he saw The carcass of a donkey whose leg had been cut open, so he said to so-and-so and so-and-so: Come closer and eat from the carcass of this donkey. They said: May God forgive you. Can a carcass be eaten? He said: “What you received from your brother is greater than that, and by the One in Whose Hand is my soul, it is among the rivers of Paradise, to be immersed in it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6892","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: I am Abd al-Razzaq, he said: Ibn Jurayj told us, he said: Abu al-Zubayr informed me, that Abd al-Rahman bin Silent Abu Hurairah’s cousin told him that he heard Abu Hurairah say: Al-Aslami came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. So he testified against himself four times of adultery, saying: I had sexual intercourse with a forbidden woman. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, turned away from all of this. So he came at the fifth time and said to him: “Did you marry her?” He said: Yes. He said: Do you know what fornication is? He said: Yes. He said: I committed a forbidden act from her. Like when a man comes from his family as permissible. He said: What do you mean by this saying? He said: I want you to purify me. He said: So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, commanded it. May God bless him and grant him peace, that he should be stoned. So he was stoned, so he heard two of his companions, one of them saying to his companion: Look at this man whom God has covered. He did not let him go, until he was stoned like a dog. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, remained silent about them. Then he walked and passed by the carcass of a paralyzed donkey. With his foot, he said: Where is so-and-so? They said: We are there, O Messenger of God. He said to them: Eat from the carcass of this donkey. They said: O Messenger of God. May God forgive you. Who eats this? Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: What you have received from this offer is worse than eating. This carcass, by the One in Whose Hand is my soul, it is now in the rivers of Paradise.”"
"6893","Muhammad bin Hatim bin Nu’aym told us, he said: I am Habban, he is the son of Musa, he said: I am Abdullah, he is Ibn al-Mubarak, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, On the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Hadad, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that a goat came to a man called: Hazal, and he said: Oh Hazal, The other one committed adultery, so what do you think? He said: Go to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, before the Qur’an is revealed to you. So he came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and informed him. That he had committed adultery, so he turned away from it, then he told him, so he turned away from it, then he told him, so he turned away from it four times, so when it was The fourth time, he ordered that he be stoned. When he was stoned, he took refuge in a tree and was killed. A man said to his companion: This is the one who was killed as a dog is killed. Then the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, came to a dead donkey and said to them: “Get rid of this donkey.” They said: O Messenger of God, it is a corpse. It is dead. How can we breathe from it? He said: What happened to your brother, by the One in whose hand is the soul of Muhammad, is that he immersed himself in rivers. Paradise, and he said to Huzal: Woe to you, Huzal! May God have mercy on him. He said: Abu Abd al-Rahman: Abd al-Rahman ibn Hihadhad is not famous, and there was disagreement over Abu al-Zubayr regarding his father’s name. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6894","Wasil bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Bashir bin Al-Muhajir, on the authority of Abdullah bin Buraidah, on the authority of his father, He said: I was sitting with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, when Al-Aslami Ma’iz bin Malik came to him and said: O Messenger of God, I committed adultery. And I want you to purify me. So he said to him: “Go back.” So he came back. Then he came to him a second time, and he said: “Go back.” So he came back. So he came to him a third time, so he came. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, asked his people, and they praised him well. He said: How is his mind? Is he mad? They said: No, by God O Messenger of God, he is true, so they praised him well for his mind and religion. Then he came to him the fourth time and asked them about him, and they said something like So he ordered them to dig a hole for him up to his chest, then stone him."
"6895","Suwayd bin Nasr told us, he said: I am Abdullah, he is Ibn Al-Mubarak, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Ikrimah, On the authority of Ibn Abbas, that Al-Aslami came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he confessed to adultery, and he said: “Perhaps you kissed, or winked, or \You looked\"""""""
"6896","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Wahb bin Jarir told me, he said: my father told me, on the authority of Ali, and Abdullah bin Al-Haytham told me Ibn Othman Al-Basri, he said: Wahb bin Jarir told us, he said: Ubayy told us, he said: I heard Ya’la bin Hakim narrating, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to Ma’iz ibn Malik: “Woe to you! Perhaps you kissed, or winked, or looked? He said: No. He said: So he joked with her? He said: Yes. He said: Then he ordered that he be stoned. Amr said in his hadith: A goat came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Perhaps you kissed, or winked, or Did you look? He said: No. He said: Did you do that? He said: Yes, O Messenger of God. So he ordered that he be stoned. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6897","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Abdul Wahhab is Al-Thaqafi told us, he said: Khaled told us, on the authority of Ikrimah, that a goat came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. And he said to him: I committed adultery, so he turned away from it, so he said it repeatedly, and he said to him: “Have you married?” He said: Yes, so he asked his people about him: Is there harm in him? Did he touch him? They said: No, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, stoned him. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6898","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Abu Awanah told us, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace He, peace and blessings of God be upon him, said to Ma’iz ibn Malik: “Is what he reported to me about you true? He said: What informed you about me? He said: I was informed that you had intercourse with the slave girl of so-and-so’s family?” He said: Yes, so he gave four testimonies, then he ordered that he be stoned.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6899","Hilal bin Al-Ala bin Hilal told me, he said: Husayn told us, and he is the trustworthy bin of Ayyash Al-Bajdadi, he said: Zuhayr told us, he said: Samak bin Harb told us. He said: Saeed bin Jubayr told me, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “It is true that Ma’iz did not inform me of you. Did you have sexual intercourse with the daughter of the son of so-and-so? He said: Yes, so he confessed four times, twice, so he stoned him."
"6900","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul Rahim Al-Barqi told us, he said: Al-Faryabi told us, he said: Israel told us, he said: Samak bin Harb told us, On the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was brought with Ma’iz bin Malik, so he confessed twice, then he said “Take him away, then return him. He confessed twice, until he confessed four times, and he said: Take him away and stone him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6901","Ahmad bin Amr bin Al-Sarh told us, he said: Ibn Wahb told us, he said: Yunus told me, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, he said: Abu Salamah told me Bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Jabir Bin Abdullah, that a man who had converted to Islam came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, while he was in the mosque. So he called him and told him that he had committed adultery, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, turned away from him, so he moved away with his brother who had turned away before him, so he told him That he committed adultery, so he testified against himself four times, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, summoned him and said: “Are you crazy?” He said: No. He said: Did you behave well? He said: Yes, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered him to be stoned in the place of prayer. Then when the stones pelted him, he fled until He caught a free woman and was killed by stoning for it."
"6902","Ibrahim bin Al-Hasan Al-Masisi told me, he said: Hajjaj told us, he said: Ibn Jurayj said: Ibn Shihab told me, on the authority of the hadith of Abu Salamah, On the authority of Jabir, that a man from Islam came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “and told him that he had committed adultery, so he bore witness against himself four times.” Testimonies, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered that he be stoned.” He had been married. They claimed that he was Ma’iz bin Malik."
"6903","Muhammad ibn Rafi’ al-Naysaburi and Nuh ibn Habib al-Qumsi informed us, saying: Abd al-Razzaq told us, he said: I am Muammar, on the authority of al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Jabir, that a man who had converted to Islam came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he confessed to adultery, so he turned away from it, then he confessed, So he turned away from it, until he testified against himself four times, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: “Is your father mad?” He said: No. He said: Have you done well? He said: Yes, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered that he be stoned in the prayer place. When the stones threw him, he fled, and he was caught up and stoned until He died, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: Good, but did not pray for him.” The wording is by Ibn Rafi’ (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6904","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak told us, he said: Hujayn narrated to us, he said: Al-Layth narrated to us, on the authority of Aqeel, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Abu Salamah, And Saeed, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, said: A Muslim man came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, while he was in the mosque, and called him, and said: “ O Messenger of God, I committed adultery, so he turned away from him, so he turned away to face him and said: O Messenger of God, I committed adultery, so he turned away from him, until This was repeated against him four times, and when he gave four testimonies against himself, he summoned him and said: Are you crying mad? He said: No. He said: Have you done well? He said: Yes. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Take him and stone him. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6905","Amr bin Mansour Al-Nasa’i told us, he said: Al-Hakam bin Nafi’ told us, he said: I am Shuaib, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, he said: Abu Salama told me, And Saeed, that Abu Hurairah said: A man came to whom the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, converted to Islam while he was in the mosque, and called him, and said: “O Messenger of By God, the other committed adultery, meaning himself, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, turned away from him, so he turned away, meaning, to split his face, which had turned away from it. He said: O Messenger of God, the other one committed adultery, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, turned away from him, so he stepped aside to cut his face, which had turned away from his. He said: O Messenger of God, the other one committed adultery, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, turned away from him, so the fourth man stepped aside for him, and when he testified against himself Four testimonies. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, called him and said: “Are you mad? He said: No, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Take him and stone him. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6906","Al-Harith bin Miskin read about it, and I hear, on the authority of Ibn al-Qasim, he said: Malik told me, on the authority of Yahya bin Sa’id, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, that a man from Aslam came to Abu Bakr Al-Siddiq and said to him: The other had committed adultery, so Abu Bakr said to him: Did you mention that? For anyone else? He said: No, so Abu Bakr said to him: Repent to God, so cover yourself with God’s cover, for God accepts repentance from His servants, so Omar came and said The same thing he said to Abu Bakr, and Omar told him what Abu Bakr told him, so he came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: The other had He committed adultery, Sa`id said: Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, turned away from it three times. He sent to his family and said: “Does he complain? Is he suffering from a disease?” They said: O Messenger of God, by God, he is healthy. So the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Abu Bakr or Thayb?” He said: “Rather Thayb.” So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered him to be stoned. Al-Hussein bin Mansour Al-Naysaburi told us, he said: Ibn Numayr told us, he said: Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, that a man He who converted to Islam went to Abu Bakr al-Siddiq and mentioned something similar to him."
"6907","Al-Hussein bin Mansour told us, he said: Ibn Numayr told us, he said: Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of another man from He converted to Islam. He mentioned to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, that he had committed adultery. “Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered that he be stoned.” Saeed mentioned that the Messenger of God prayed over one of them."
"6908","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Muhammad told us, he said: I am Shu`bah, on the authority of Simak, he said: I heard Jabir bin Samra, saying: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came May God bless him and grant him peace, a short, disheveled, muscular man, wearing a garment, who had committed adultery, so he repeated it twice, then ordered him to be stoned.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6909","Hilal bin Al-Ala told us, he said: Husayn told us, he said: Zuhayr told us, he said: Samak bin Harb told us, he said: Jabir bin Samra told me, he said: He came Ma'iz bin Malik Al-Aslami, a short man in a garment, with no robe over him, and I was looking at him. He said: And the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Leaning on a pillow to his left, he said: There were people between me and him, so he spoke to him, and I do not know what he was speaking to, while I was watching. Then he said: “ “Take him away.” So he took him off, then he said: “Send him back.” He responded, so he spoke to him, then he said: “Take him away and stone him.”"
"6910","Amr bin Mansour Al-Nasa’i told me, he said: Harami bin Hafs told me, he said: Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Ulatha told us, he said: Abd told us. Al-Aziz bin Omar bin Abdul-Aziz, that Khalid bin Al-Lajlaj told him that his father Al-Lajlaj told him that he was sitting and praying in The market, and a woman passed by carrying a boy, and the people revolted, and I revolted over who revolted, so I came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: “Who Is this man’s father with you? She remained silent. Then a young man wearing her shoe said: I am his father, O Messenger of God. He approached her and said: Who is this man’s father with you? She remained silent Then the boy said: She is young in age, very young, shameful, and she is not one of your words. I am his father. So he looked at some of his friends. It was as if he was asking them about it, and they said: We knew nothing but good, or something like that, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: Did you do good? He said: Yes So he ordered that he be stoned. He said: So we took him out, and we dug for him until we were able, then we threw stones at him until he calmed down, then we departed to... While we were sitting there, an old man came asking about the person who had been stoned, so we went up to him, took hold of his clothes, and set off with him. To the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and we said: O Messenger of God, this is being asked about the evil. So the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Mah, it is better in the sight of God than the scent of musk.” So we left with the sheikh, and behold, it was his father. We came to him, so we helped him to Washing him and shrouding him. He said: I do not know whether to pray for him or not. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6911","Ahmad bin Al-Mu'alla bin Yazid Al-Dimashqi told us, saying: Suleiman bin Abdul-Rahman and Abdul-Rahman bin Ibrahim told us, saying: Al-Walid told us. He is Ibn Muslim. He said: Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Sha’ithi told us, on the authority of Maslama bin Abdullah Al-Juhani, on the authority of Khaled bin Al-Lajlaj, on the authority of His father, he said: We were working in the market, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered a man to be stoned. Then a man came to him and asked us to guide him to... The place where he was stoned, so we clung to him, until we brought him to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and we said: O Messenger of God, this one came. To ask us about that evil person whom you stoned today. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Do not say: evil, for by God he is “Better in the sight of God than musk.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6912","Ibrahim bin Yaqoub Al-Jawzjani told me, he said: Yahya bin Ya’la bin Al-Harith told us, he said: Ubayy told us, he said: Ghaylan bin Jami’ told us, On the authority of Alqamah ibn Marthad, on the authority of Sulayman ibn Buraydah, on the authority of his father, he said: A Ghamidi woman from Azd came and said: O Messenger of God Purify me. He said: “Woe to you! Go back and ask God for forgiveness, and repent to Him.” She said: “Perhaps you want to return me as you rejected Ma’iz bin Malik?” He said: What is that? She said: She became pregnant as a result of adultery. He said: Are you married? She said: Yes. He said: Not until you give birth to what is in your womb. He said: So a man from Ansar, until she gave birth, and he came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: Al-Ghamidiyah has given birth, so he said: Then we will not stone her, and we will leave Her child was small and he had no one to breastfeed him, so a man from the Ansar stood up and said: May he be breastfed, O Prophet of God, so he stoned her.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6913","Muhammad ibn Ali ibn al-Hasan ibn Shaqiq informed me, he said: My father informed us, he said: I am Abu Hamza Muhammad ibn Maimun al-Marwazi al-Sukkari, on the authority of Ibrahim Al-Sayegh, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, that a woman came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: I have committed adultery, so carry out the punishment for me. He said: “Go until you wean your child.” When she weaned her child, she came and said: O Messenger of God, I have committed adultery, so carry out the punishment on me. He said: “Bring someone to sponsor your child.” Then a man stood up and said: “I will sponsor her child, O Messenger of God.” He stoned her. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6914","Ishaq bin Mansour Al-Maruzi told us, he said: I am Muhammad bin Yusuf, he said: Al-Awza’i told us, he said: Yahya told me, he said: Abu told me Qalaba, on the authority of Abu Al-Muhajir, on the authority of Imran, he said: A woman came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: “O Messenger of God, I befriended someone, so appoint him as my guardian. He called her guardian and said: Be kind to this woman until she puts what is in her stomach. When she puts what is in her stomach, Her stomach, so bring her, and when she gave birth to what was in her stomach, she was brought to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered that May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, so her clothes were torn on her, then he ordered that she be stoned, then he prayed over her, and they said: O Messenger of God, should you pray over her? She committed adultery? He said: She has repented so much that if it were divided among seventy, it would be sufficient for them. Can she find anything better than that she tried to please herself? “For God’s sake?” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6915","Ismail bin Masoud told us, he said: Khalid, who is the son of Harith, told us, he said: Hisham, who is the son of Sanbar al-Distawai, told us, on the authority of Yahya On the authority of Abu Qilaba, on the authority of Abu al-Muhallab, on the authority of Imran bin Husayn, that a woman from Juhayna came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, She said: “I have committed adultery, and she is pregnant.” So he handed her over to her guardian, and he said: “Be good to her, and when she gives birth, bring her to me.” When she gave birth, he came. So he ordered her to be put together, then he stoned her, then he prayed over her. Omar said to him: Are you praying over her when she has committed adultery? So he said to him: She has repented to such a degree that, if it were divided among seventy of the people of the city, it would be enough for them. Can she find anything better than that she sacrificed herself? \For God's sake.\"" Abu Abdul Rahman said: Abu Al-Muhajir is wrong"
"6916","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Abdullah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, and Zaid bin Khalid and Shibl said: We were with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and a man came up to him and said: I adjure you by God, have you decided between us according to a letter? God, then his opponent stood up, and he was more understanding than him, and he said: He has spoken the truth, yes, judge between us according to the Book of God. He said: “Say, he said: My son was violent towards This man committed adultery with his wife, so I ransomed him from him with a hundred sheep and a servant, as if he had been told that his son should be stoned, so I ransomed him from him, then I asked men of knowledge, and they told me that my son must be subjected to one hundred lashes and a year’s exile, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: “ By the One in whose hand is my soul, I will judge between you according to the Book of God: a hundred sheep and a servant shall be returned to you, and your son shall receive a hundred lashes, and exile for a year. Go tomorrow, O Unais, to this woman. If she confesses, stone her.” So he went to her, and she confessed, and he stoned her. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6917","Qutaibah bin Saeed informed us, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Abdullah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, and Zaid bin Khaled Al-Juhani, that they told him that two men disputed with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and one of them said: Judge between us. With the Book of God, and the other one, who was the most understanding of them, said: O Messenger of God, allow me to speak. He said: “Speak.” He said: “Indeed, my son was stubborn.” Because of this, he committed adultery with his wife. They told me that my son should be stoned, so I ransomed him with a hundred sheep and a female slave. Then I asked the people of Knowledge, so they told me that my son does not have to suffer a hundred lashes, and he mentioned a word that means: general exile, but the stoning is imposed on his wife, so he said The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, I will judge between you according to the Book of God. As for your sheep and your female servant, it will be returned to you.” He flogged his son a hundred, and exiled him for a year, and ordered Unais to go to the other's wife, and if she confessed, he would stone her, and she confessed. So he stoned her"
"6918","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Abdullah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, and Zaid bin Khalid, that they said: A man of the Bedouins came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: O Messenger of God, I implore you to decree for me in writing. God, so the other opponent, who was more understanding than him, said: Yes, so judge between us according to the Book of God, and give me permission. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Say, he said: My son was stubborn because of this, so he committed adultery with his wife, and I was informed that my son should be stoned, so I ransomed him with a hundred sheep. And a child, so I asked the people of knowledge, and they told me that my son is liable for a hundred lashes, and a general banishment, and that this woman is required, stoning, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “By the One in whose hand is my soul, I will decide between you by the Book of God, the female offspring and the sheep shall be returned, and the Your son will receive a hundred lashes, and exile for a year. Tomorrow, O Unays, go to this woman, and if she confesses, stone her.” So he attacked her and she confessed. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered her to be stoned."
"6919","Salama bin Shabib Al-Naysaburi told us, on the authority of Qudama bin Muhammad, he said: Makhramah bin Bukayr told us, on the authority of his father, he said: I heard Amr bin Shuaib, who said: I heard Muhammad bin Muslim bin Shihab, who said: I heard Ubayd Allah bin Abdullah, saying: I heard Abu Hurairah, saying: He came Two men went to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: O Messenger of God, decide between me and this man. My son was his wife’s employee, and my son did not We won it, so I asked those who did not know, and they told me that my son should be stoned, so I ransomed him with such-and-such, then I asked who He knows, so they informed me that stoning is not required of my son. The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “I will judge between you with justice. As for what I gave him,” he responded. On you, and as for your son, we will give him one hundred lashes, and he will be absent for a year, and as for his wife, she will be stoned.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6920","Muhammad ibn Rafi’ al-Naysaburi told us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq told us, he said: I am Muammar, on the authority of Yahya, he is the son of Abi Kathir, on the authority of Abu Qalaba On the authority of Abu Al-Muhallab, on the authority of Imran bin Husayn, that a woman from Juhayna confessed to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, about adultery, and she said: I She became pregnant, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, called her guardian and said to him: “Be good to her, and when she gives birth, inform me.” He did so, and informed The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, caused her to fall into disrepair, then he ordered her to be stoned, so she was stoned, then he prayed over her.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6921","Mahmoud bin Khaled Al-Dimashqi told me, on the authority of Al-Walid, meaning Ibn Muslim. He said: Abu Amr told me, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of my father Qalabah, on the authority of Abu Al-Muhajir, on the authority of Imran bin Husayn, that a woman came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and confessed to adultery, so he ordered her to The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and her clothes were tied around her, meaning he pulled her clothes around her, then he stoned her, then he prayed over her.” Job sent him (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6922","Muhammad bin Hatim bin Nu’aym told us, he said: I am Habban, he is the son of Musa, he said: I am Abdullah, on the authority of Zakaria Abi Imran Al-Basri, he said: I heard a sheikh, speaking to Amr bin Othman Al-Qurashi, who said: Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Bakra told us, on the authority of his father, who said: I witnessed the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He greeted him while he was standing on his mule, when a pregnant woman came to him and said: She has committed a sin, so stone her. The Prophet said to her, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace: “Take cover with God’s protection.” So she went and returned to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, while he was standing on his mule. She said: Stone her, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Cover yourself with God’s protection. So she returned, then the third time came, and he was standing on His mule, and she took the reins and said: I adjure you by God, do not stone her. He said: Go, I have a son. So she went and gave birth to a boy. She brought him to the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, took care of him. Then he said: Go, and purify yourself of the blood. So she set off. So she was cleansed of the blood, then she came, so the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, sent for women, and he ordered them to seek permission from her, and to see Was she cleansed of blood? So they came and testified before the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, that she had been cleansed. Then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered a pit to be made for her. Then he and the Muslims approached, and he said with his hand, and he took a pebble that looked like a chickpea, or something like a chickpea, and he threw it. Then he said to the Muslims: Throw it, and beware of its face. So they threw it until it calmed down, so they were ordered to take it out, and he prayed over it. Then he said: If only Its reward was divided among the people of Hijaz, to accommodate them.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6923","Ahmad bin Yahya al-Sufi Kufi told me, he said: Abu Nu`aym told us, he said: Bashir bin Muhajir told us, he said: Abdullah bin Buraydah told us, on the authority of His father, he said: I was sitting with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, when a woman came to him and said: O Prophet of God, I have committed adultery, and I I want you to purify me, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to her: “Go back.” The next day, she went to him and confessed to him about adultery. “O Prophet of God, purify me. Perhaps you want to return me as you rejected Ma’iz bin Malik. By God, I am pregnant.” The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to her. He said: Go back until you give birth. When she gave birth, she brought him the boy, carrying him in a cloth, and said: O Prophet of God, this is what you have given birth to. He said: So go and breastfeed him until you wean him. When she had weaned him, she brought the boy with a piece of bread in his hand, and said: O Prophet of God, this has I weaned him, so he ordered the boy to be taken, so he gave him to a man of the Muslims, and he ordered her to be dug for her, and she was placed in it facing her chest, then He ordered the people to stone her, so Khalid ibn al-Walid approached with a stone and threw it at her, and blood splattered on Khaled’s face or forehead, and he cursed her. Then the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, heard him cursing her, so he said: Wait, Khaled, do not curse her, for by the One in whose hand is my soul, she has repented with complete repentance. If a tax owner had repented of her, it would have been accepted from him, so he ordered it to be done, prayed over it, and buried it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6924","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik ibn Abi al-Shawareb al-Basri informed us, on the authority of Yazid, who was Ibn Zurayi. He said: Dawud told us, on the authority of Abu Nadra, On the authority of Abu Saeed, that Ma’iz bin Malik came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: I committed an indecent act, and he mentioned a word that means: He returned it repeatedly. So he asked his people: “Is there harm in him? It was said: There is no harm in him. So he commanded us, so we went with him to Baqi’ al-Gharqad, but we did not dig for him, nor did we We bound him, and we threw potsherds and cast iron at him, and he ran, and we hastened after him, and he came to Al-Hurra. Then he mentioned words that meant: So he stood up for us, and we threw him. With boulders, until he was still.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6925","Abdul Rahman bin Khalid Al-Raqi told us, he said: Muawiyah bin Hisham told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Dawud bin Abi Hind, on the authority of Abu Nadhrah, on the authority of Abu Sa’id, who said: Ma’iz bin Malik came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he confessed to adultery four times, so he asked about it."
"6926","Quraysh bin Abdul Rahman Bawardi told me, Ali bin Al Hassan told us, he said: I am Al Hussein, he is Ibn Waqid, he said: Abu Al Zubair told me He said: Abd al-Rahman bin al-Hidhab, the son of my brother Abu Hurairah, told me. He said: I heard Abu Hurairah saying: A man went to the Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: O Prophet of God, I have committed adultery. He said: “Woe to you! Do you know what fornication is?” He said: Yes, it afflicts a man with a woman who does not It is permissible for him, just as it befalls his family. So he said to him: Go. He turned him back. He passed by a man called Al-Hazzaal, and he said: Did you not see that I came to the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him? May God bless him and grant him peace. I said: O Prophet of God, I have committed adultery. He said to me: Oh, woe to you. Do you know what adultery is? I said: Yes, it can befall a man A woman who is not permissible for him, just as it happens to his family, and he brought me back and said to him: Go back to him, so he came to him and said to him: O Prophet of God, I I committed adultery. He said: Yes, woe to you. Do you know what adultery is? He said: Yes, it happens to a man from a woman who is not permissible for him, just as it happens to his family. He said: To him: Go, so he sent him back, and he came to the emaciated man, and said to him: Go back to him. So he returned to him and said to him: O Prophet of God, I have committed adultery. He said: Yes, woe to you. Do you know what adultery is? He said something like that, so he returned it, and he came to him and said: Go back to it. He returned to him the fourth time and said: O Prophet of God! I have committed adultery. He said: Yes, woe to you. Do you know what adultery is? He said: Yes, it happens to a man from a woman who is not permissible for him, just as it happens to his family. He said to him: Did you enter and leave? He said: Yes. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: May you be cursed for the rest of the day. So he ordered that he be stoned, and said: He was destroyed by emaciation, three times. He said: He was stoned. Then he reached the root of a tree, where he lay down and leaned on his right hand, until he was killed. Then two men from... The Companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and they said: Look at this man who came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He turned him all away, but he refused except to He can be killed like a dog! So the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, heard it, and he passed by a dead donkey with its leg bent, and he said: O these two, come and eat. They said: O Prophet of God, will you Can anyone eat from this? ! He said: What you have received before from your brother was worse than this, and by the One in Whose Hand is my soul, I saw him bathing among the rivers of Paradise. He said: It means to enjoy (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6927","Ahmad ibn Harb told us, he said: Qasim ibn Yazid, who is the father of Yazid al-Jarmi, there is nothing wrong with him, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Salamah ibn Kuhail He said: Abu Malik told me, on the authority of a man from the companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: Ma’iz bin Malik came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He greeted him four times, and each time he returned him and said: “Did you tell anyone but me?” Then he ordered that he be stoned, and they took him to a place about He threw his chest to a wall, and he started jumping, and a man threw it at him, hitting the roots of his ears, so he was struck down and killed him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6928","Ahmad bin Yahya al-Sufi al-Kufi told me, he said: Abu Nu`aym told me, he said: Bashir bin al-Muhajir al-Ghanawi told me, he said: Abdullah bin told me. Buraidah, on the authority of his father, said: I was sitting with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, when a man called Ma’iz bin Malik came and said: Oh Messenger of God, I have committed adultery, and I want you to purify me. So the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: “Go back.” And the next day, he came to him again. So he confessed to him about adultery, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: Go back. Then he sent to his people and asked them about him, and he said: What Do you know of Ma'iz ibn Malik? Do you see any harm in him, or do you deny something about his intelligence? They said: O Prophet of God, we see no harm in him? And we did not deny anything about his mind. Then he returned to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, the third time, and he confessed to him about adultery and said: O Prophet of God, Purify me, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, also sent to his people and asked them about him, and they said as they said the first time: What do we see in him? He was brave, and we did not deny anything about his mind. Then he returned to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, the fourth time, and he also confessed to him about adultery, so the Prophet ordered May God bless him and grant him peace. So a pit was dug for him, and he was placed in it up to his chest. Then he ordered the people to stone him.” Buraydah said: We were talking with the companions of the Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, that if a goat sat on its saddle three times after his confession, He did not ask for him, but stoned him at four o'clock. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6929","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Harami bin Hafs Abu Ali told us, he said: Ibn Ulathah told us, he said: Abd al-Aziz bin Omar bin told me. Abdul Aziz, that Khalid bin Al-Lajlaj told him that his father told him, he said: I was working, and a woman passed by with a boy, So the people revolted, and I revolted over whoever revolted, so I ended up with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said to the woman: “Who is the father of this boy?” She remained silent, he said. A young man stood up and said: I am his father, O Messenger of God. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Who is this boy’s father? The boy said: I am His father, O Messenger of God, and she is young in age, recent, meaning, a covenant with disgrace, and it is not what you said. I am his father, O Messenger of God. It was as if he looked at those around him and asked them: What do you say? They said: We know nothing but good. He said: Did you do good? He said: Yes, so he ordered that he be stoned. So we took him and dug for him, and, if possible, we threw him until he calmed down.” . . The chain of the hadith (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6930","Ahmad bin Sulaiman Al-Rahawi told us, he said: Yazid bin Harun told us, he said: I am Muhammad bin Amr, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, He said: Ma'iz bin Malik came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: O Messenger of God, I have committed adultery, so he turned away from it, then He came to him from his right side and said: O Messenger of God, I have committed adultery. He said that four times. He said: “Go with him and stone him.” So they went. With it, when the stones touched him, he turned around to fight hard, and a man met him with a camel’s jaw in his hand. He struck him and knocked him down. He mentioned that to the Messenger of God. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He fled when the stones touched him. He said: “Will you not leave him alone?” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
